          window.googletag = window.googletag || { cmd: [] }
        </script><script type="text/javascript">window.cns = window.cns || {}; window.cns.pageContext = {"channel":"skin-care","content":{"copyCount":1503,"imageCount":0,"embedCount":41,"inline_embed_total":41,"ratio":36.65853658536585,"midContentCadence":500,"adCount":null},"contentType":"article","experiments":{"bucketLabel":[],"experimentLabel":[],"payload":[]},"adsExperiments":{"status":200,"features":{"paywall-gate":{"defaultValue":{}}},"experiments":[],"dateUpdated":"2026-09-02T12:33:31.539Z"},"functionalTags":["annieblay-ed","diannamazzone-ed","commerce"],"targeting":{"cnt_copilotid":["67915d9475d8c2a6a29b44d4"],"cnt_platform":["verso"],"cnt_tags":["skin","shopping","k-beauty","skin-care"],"feature_flags":[]},"server":"production","slug":"korean-beauty-founders-favorite-products","subChannel":"","subSubChannel":"","templateType":"mt_commerce_article_two_column"};</script><link rel="preconnect" href="https://ads-static.conde.digital"/><script id="ads-v6" src="https://ads-static.conde.digital/production/cns/builds/allure/v6.js?v=13279" async=""></script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"NewsArticle","articleBody":"If Korea stands as the capital of the skin-care kingdom, then the founders of K-beauty brands are its faithful guards. These business-savvy, well-moisturized individuals (including Alicia Yoon of Peach & Lily, Liah Yoo of KraveBeauty, and Charlotte Cho of Then I Met You) are experts among experts. So in an eager desire to be further in the know about the hi-tech treatments, souped-up formulas, and innovative ingredients coming out of Korea, we asked them to share the K-beauty products on regular rotation in their own routines. Of course, they have favorites within their own brands, but we also asked them what other K-beauty products they swear by—like, is there a secret, under-the-radar serum that gives them enviable glass skin?\nDespite the heralded 10-step Korean skin-care routine, most of these founders keep their beauty routines fairly simple, focusing on hydration and barrier maintenance—with a few special additions that eliminate texture, purify the skin, and of course, induce a healthy glow. And since the focus of their regimens is on skin care, many tend to keep their makeup minimal—using products that subtly enhance their natural features, like glossy lip tints and lightweight cushion foundations.\nKeep reading for the products your (and our) favorite K-beauty founders use on the daily.\nChristine Chang, Co-CEO of Glow Recipe\nA big component of Christine Chang’s beauty routine is prepping her skin for makeup—though on most occasions you may not even be able to tell that Chang is wearing any. She prepares her skin for seamless application using her own Glow Recipe Watermelon Glow Niacinamide Dew Drops. “This serum is my daily niacinamide treatment but it creates such a beautiful, emollient base for any makeup and makes the morning routine so easy,” says Chang.\nTo even out her complexion, Chang uses the Black Cushion Foundation from the popular Korean makeup brand Hera. “I’ve been testing different cushions and have liked the glowy finish and easy application [from this one],” Chang tells Allure.\nGlossy lip products had a big moment last year, and Chang was not immune to the hype—though instead of the popular glosses and tinted balms that went viral stateside, Chang fell in love with the Korean makeup brand Amuse’s Dew Tint. “I picked up different tints at Olive Young during a recent trip to Korea and it’s been fun to play and test,” says Chang.\nCharlotte Cho, founder of SokoGlam and Then I Met You\nHydration, hydration, and hydration are three words that describe Charlotte Cho’s skin-care routine. After double cleansing, the SokoGlam founder uses the Real Barrier Intense Moisture Toner, which has seven different types of hyaluronic acid wrapped up in one milky formula. She follows that up with the Torriden Dive Serum—with hyaluronic acid and allantoin—and her own Then I Met You Bong2 Bounce Cream. “It’s a citrusy moisturizer that not only smells like a dream but also does an incredible job of protecting your skin barrier,” says Cho.\nLast but never least, Cho ends her morning skincare routine with her beloved IOPE Air Cushion SPF 50. “I've been using the IOPE Air Cushion for years—since IOPE invented cushion technology,” says Cho. “[Using it is] the only way my foundation looks airbrushed and not cakey.”\nSarah Lee, Co-CEO of Glow Recipe\nThe other half of the Glow Recipe founding duo, Sarah Lee, says her personal MVP among the brand’s lineup is Watermelon Glow PHA + BHA Pore-Tight Toner. Lee tells Allure that the toner was inspired by Korean aqua peel facials—a treatment that involves coating the skin in a water-based gel and using a suctioning device to exfoliate and remove dirt and debris (where do we sign up?).\nLee also uses an essence—which is not to be confused with a toner, which provides gentle exfoliation—for a hydration boost. “I love using the Mixsoon Bean Essence as my serum step because it offers great hydration and skin-plumping benefits,” says Lee.\nWhen it comes to makeup, Lee keeps it simple but always reaches for the Clio Black Eyeliner. “I have been using eyeliners from Clio for years as it’s the number one black eyeliner in Korea,’ says Lee. This water-proof pencil has a two millimeter-thin tip that makes creating sharp precise liner look effortless.\nYanghee Paik, co-founder of Rael Beauty\nRunning an international skin- and feminine- care brand is no easy feat, but Yanghee Paik always looks fresh while doing it thanks to a curated collection of K-beauty products.\nHer arsenal includes her own Rael Beauty Miracle Clear Exfoliating Cleanser, which Paik uses every day to help fend off breakouts without stripping her skin. Another blemish-banishing product Paik keeps on hand is Numbuzin No. 5+ Vitamin Glutathione Ampoule. “Recently, glutathione [a combination of amino acids glycine, cysteine, and glutamic acid] has gained a lot of popularity in K-beauty for targeting blemish scars and hyperpigmentation,” says Paik.\nMakeup-wise, Paik reaches for rom&nd Blur Fudge Tint and Dear Dahlia Timeless Bloom Collection Palette. “I use the lip tint almost every day for its natural finish,” says Paik. “I discovered Dear Dahlia while searching for vegan and cruelty-free cosmetic brands in Korea and fell in love with its eyeshadow palette. The shadows feel very gentle and smooth on the delicate eye area.”\nJu Rhyu, co-founder of Hero Cosmetics\nJu Rhyu wasted no time letting us know that Korean sunscreens are her favorite K-beauty product. “I love Beauty of Joseon and Roundlab Birch Moisturizer,” says Rhyu of her top SPFs. “They are so lightweight and water-based that they are a joy to apply—and [they’re] affordable. I use them after moisturizer and before makeup to protect my skin every day.”\nBefore excitedly slathering on SPF, Rhyu uses Superegg Vitality Elixir. “It's a nice antioxidant serum by Erica Choi and Hoon Kim. I use it before my SPF to ensure added protection from free radicals,” says Rhyu.\nThe Hero co-founder and CEO also has a “renewed appreciation” for luxury K-beauty brand Sulwhasoo. ”I really enjoy the Sulwhasoo Concentrated Ginseng Renewing Cream for when my skin needs more moisture on drier days,” says Rhyu.\nRhyu also reaches for her own Hero Cosmetics Mighty Patch Original when she needs to fight off a blemish—just like we do. We gave the patches a 2024 Best of Beauty award.\nLiah Yoo, founder of KraveBeauty\nYou’ve likely come across at least one of KraveBeauty’s viral products on TikTok—perhaps the Best of Beauty-winning Beet The Sun SPF 40. If you love it as much as we do, you have Liah Yoo to thank.\nYoo starts her own routine by cleansing with Experiment Beauty Plasma Wash. “I usually have low expectations for cleansers, but this one completely blew me away,” says Yoo. “After using it, my skin feels like it’s been treated to a hydrating mask.”\nYoo also loves Goodal Green Tangerine Vitamin C Serum for brightening and evening out her skin tone. “It’s super gentle, even for sensitive skin, and the vitamin C works wonders to give my complexion a radiant boost,” says Yoo.\nShe also uses her own KraveBeauty Oil La La serum religiously, calling it “gentle yet effective” and pointing to its blend of linoleic acid-rich oils including rosehip seed, jojoba, sunflower, and grapeseed.\nAlicia Yoon, founder and CEO of Peach & Lily\nThe double cleansing method—as in, washing your face with an oil-based cleanser followed by a water-based one—was popularized by K-beauty brands, so it’s no surprise that Peach & Lily founder Alicia Yoon starts her skin-care routine off her routine with this technique, first using her brand’s Ginger Melt Oil Cleanser. “I love that this effortlessly dissolves all makeup and stubborn SPF without any residue or breaking me out or making my eyes foggy,” says Yoon. (Allure editors can also vouch for Ginger Melt’s mighty cleansing power—we deemed it a 2024 Best of Beauty winner.)\nPart two of Yoon’s double cleansing routine features Peach Slices Snail Rescue Purifying Cleanser before she moves on to the rest of her regimen, which includes K-beauty powerhouse products like Mimu Mimu Cooling Calming Toner (a cooling, cica-based toner from a new Korean skin-care brand), NYBG Skincare Serum (a firming serum created by Yoon’s dermatologist, Dr. Choi Won Woo), and Eco Your Skin Meso Ampoule which contains micro spicules: microscopic sharp, crystalline structures that come from sea sponges and provide a gentle exfoliating effect.\n“Before micro spicules in serums became trendy in Korea, Eco Your Skin's OG micro spicule serum was already beloved by A-listers that frequent their spa, which happens to be Seoul's largest spa,” says Yoon, who uses the ampoule twice a week for even-toned, calm, and radiant skin.\n\nDiscover more K-Beauty stories:\n\nThe Best Korean Body-Care Products, According to K-Beauty Enthusiasts\nThe Best Korean Cleansers to Hydrate, Exfoliate, and Remove Makeup\n14 Best Korean Sunscreens for a Transparent, Glassy Finish\n\n\nNow, watch The ‘XO Kitty’ cast spill secrets:","isBasedOn":"","articleSection":"skin","author":[{"@type":"Person","name":"Annie Blay-Tettey","sameAs":"https://www.allure.com/contributor/annie-blay"}],"dateModified":"2025-01-28T09:00:00.000-05:00","datePublished":"2025-01-28T09:00:00.000-05:00","headline":"7 K-Beauty Founders Share Their Favorite Products","image":["https://media.allure.com/photos/6797f1d402c227dcaa0298d4/16:9/w_3488,h_1962,c_limit/Allure_7%20K-Beauty%20Founders_3500x2000.jpg","https://media.allure.com/photos/6797f1d402c227dcaa0298d4/4:3/w_2314,h_1736,c_limit/Allure_7%20K-Beauty%20Founders_3500x2000.jpg","https://media.allure.com/photos/6797f1d402c227dcaa0298d4/1:1/w_2000,h_2000,c_limit/Allure_7%20K-Beauty%20Founders_3500x2000.jpg"],"inLanguage":"en-US","keywords":["skin","shopping","k-beauty","_annieblay_ed","_diannamazzone_ed","_commerce","textaboveleftsmall","web"],"thumbnailUrl":"https://media.allure.com/photos/6797f1d402c227dcaa0298d4/2:3/w_1093,h_1639,c_limit/Allure_7%20K-Beauty%20Founders_3500x2000.jpg","url":"https://www.allure.com/story/korean-beauty-founders-favorite-products","isPartOf":{"@type":"CreativeWork","name":"Allure"},"isAccessibleForFree":true,"alternativeHeadline":"We asked seven founders of K-beauty brands including Glow Recipe, Peach & Lily, and Then I Met You to share their favorite products—and the roundup is as impressive as you’d imagine. Check out their top essences, ampoules, and milky toners, ahead.","description":"We asked seven founders of K-beauty brands including Glow Recipe, Peach & Lily, and Then I Met You to share their favorite products—and the roundup is as impressive as you’d imagine. Check out their top essences, ampoules, and milky toners, ahead.","mainEntityOfPage":{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.allure.com/story/korean-beauty-founders-favorite-products"},"publisher":{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"Allure","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://www.allure.com/verso/static/allure-us/assets/logo-seo.png","width":"618px","height":"180px"},"url":"https://www.allure.com"}}</script><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org/","@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Skin","item":"https://www.allure.com/skin-care"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"skin","item":"https://www.allure.com/topic/skin"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":3,"name":"7 K-Beauty Founders Share Their Beauty MVPs"}]}</script><script type="text/javascript" id="journey" src="https://www.allure.com/hqe4ksrs5r4Vc49I3oOBfwsJrjG_VktUWpHLRxXQsTiBrYJUb9uApteYv0gEH-Y9jdk20JFvxCpkdCRyfj7g57vEgIR2LlQaF0VmLPJIlaheJt2XUIP5LVDKvuYvroTHUF" defer=""></script><script type="text/javascript" data-testid="growthbook-script">(function (props) {
        const { userAuthenticated, section, contentType, hasBuyButtons, clientSdkKey, apiHost, enableClient, brandSlug } = props;
        const CookieAttributes = {
            AMG_USER_PARTNER: 'amg_user_partner',
            CN_XID: 'CN_xid',
            CN_SEGMENTS: 'CN_segments',
            CN_GROUPS: 'CN_groups',
            CN_GEO_COUNTRY_CODE: 'CN_geo_country_code',
            CN_DEBUG: 'cn-debug'
        };
        function extractExperimentData(experiment, result) {
            return {
                experiment_id: experiment.key,
                feature_id: result.featureId || '',
                variation: result.key,
                variation_name: result.name || '',
                payload: result.value
            };
        }
        function updateDataLayer(expDataLayer) {
            if (!Array.isArray(window.dataLayer) ||
                typeof window.dataLayer[0] !== 'object' ||
                expDataLayer.length === 0) {
                return;
            }
            const mergeAssignments = (newAssignments = [], existingAssignments = []) => {
                const merged = [...existingAssignments];
                newAssignments.forEach((newAssignment) => {
                    const existingIndex = merged.findIndex((existing) => existing.experiment_id === newAssignment.experiment_id);
                    if (existingIndex >= 0) {
                        merged[existingIndex] = newAssignment;
                    }
                    else {
                        merged.push(newAssignment);
                    }
                });
                return merged;
            };
            window.dataLayer[0].experiments = mergeAssignments(expDataLayer, window.dataLayer[0].experiments || []);
            if (window.cns) {
                const { experiments } = window.dataLayer[0];
                const { pageContext } = window.cns;
                if (experiments && experiments.length) {
                    pageContext.experiments = formatExperimentsForPageContext(experiments);
                }
            }
            const kendraGrowthBook = window.Kendra.GROWTHBOOK;
            if (kendraGrowthBook && kendraGrowthBook.broadcast) {
                kendraGrowthBook.broadcast('experiments.assignments.processed');
            }
        }
        function formatExperimentsForPageContext(experiments) {
            if (!experiments.length) {
                return {};
            }
            const bucketLabel = [];
            const experimentLabel = [];
            const payloadArray = [];
            experiments.forEach((experiment) => {
                const { variation_name, experiment_id, payload } = experiment;
                bucketLabel.push(`${variation_name}`);
                experimentLabel.push(`${experiment_id}`);
                if (Array.isArray(payload)) {
                    payloadArray.push(...payload);
                }
                else if (payload) {
                    payloadArray.push(payload);
                }
            });
            return {
                bucketLabel,
                experimentLabel,
                payload: payloadArray
            };
        }
        function perfMark(name) {
            if (typeof window.performance !== 'undefined' &&
                typeof window.performance.mark !== 'undefined') {
                window.performance.mark(name);
            }
        }
        function perfMeasure(name, startMark, endMark) {
            if (typeof window.performance !== 'undefined' &&
                typeof window.performance.measure !== 'undefined') {
                try {
                    window.performance.measure(name, startMark, endMark);
                }
                catch (e) {
                    console.error(`Error setting performance measure: ${e}`);
                }
            }
        }
        function getCookie(name) {
            if (typeof document === 'undefined' || !name) {
                return '';
            }
            const cookiePieces = document.cookie.split(/;\s?/);
            let cookieValue = '';
            for (let i = 0; i < cookiePieces.length; i++) {
                const parts = cookiePieces[i].split('=');
                if (parts[0] === name) {
                    cookieValue = decodeURIComponent(parts.slice(1).join('='));
                    break;
                }
            }
            return cookieValue;
        }
        /**
         * Decode CN_groups JWT and extract user groups
         * Supports both v1 (array of {id}) and v2 (object with category arrays) structures
         */
        function getUserGroupsFromJwt() {
            try {
                const token = getCookie(CookieAttributes.CN_GROUPS);
                if (!token)
                    return [];
                const parts = token.split('.');
                if (parts.length !== 3)
                    return [];
                // Decode header to get version
                const header = JSON.parse(atob(parts[0].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')));
                const ver = header?.ver;
                // Decode payload
                const payload = JSON.parse(atob(parts[1].replace(/-/g, '+').replace(/_/g, '/')));
                const groups = payload?.groups;
                if (!groups)
                    return [];
                let ids = [];
                if (ver === 1) {
                    // v1: groups is array of {id, rules}
                    if (Array.isArray(groups)) {
                        ids = groups
                            .map((g) => g?.id)
                            .filter((id) => typeof id === 'string');
                    }
                }
                else if (ver === 2) {
                    // v2: groups is object with category keys (ds, td, referral, etc.)
                    if (typeof groups === 'object' && !Array.isArray(groups)) {
                        ids = Object.values(groups)
                            .filter(Array.isArray)
                            .flat()
                            .filter((id) => typeof id === 'string');
                    }
                }
                return ids;
            }
            catch (e) {
                console.error('Error decoding CN_groups JWT:', e);
                return [];
            }
        }
        const isDesktopBrowser = () => {
            const { userAgent } = navigator;
            return !/Android|webOS|iPhone|iPad|iPod|BlackBerry|IEMobile|Opera Mini/i.test(userAgent);
        };
        const localStorageXidCleanUp = (prefix, xid) => {
            if (!xid) {
                return;
            }
            for (let i = 0; i < localStorage.length; i++) {
                const key = window.localStorage.key(i);
                if (key && key.startsWith(prefix) && !key.includes(xid)) {
                    window.localStorage.removeItem(key);
                }
            }
        };
        const isMobile = !isDesktopBrowser();
        const userXid = getCookie(CookieAttributes.CN_XID);
        try {
            const segment = getCookie(CookieAttributes.CN_SEGMENTS) || null;
            const userGroups = getUserGroupsFromJwt();
            const amgUserPartner = getCookie(CookieAttributes.AMG_USER_PARTNER) || '';
            const countryCode = getCookie(CookieAttributes.CN_GEO_COUNTRY_CODE) || '';
            window.growthbook_config = window.growthbook_config || {};
            const { userAgent } = navigator;
            window.growthbook_config.attributes = {
                userAgent,
                id: userXid,
                url: window.location.href,
                height: window.innerHeight,
                width: window.innerWidth,
                isMobile,
                loggedIn: userAuthenticated,
                segment,
                userGroups,
                section,
                contentType,
                hasBuyButtons,
                amgUserPartner,
                countryCode,
                brandSlug
            };
            window.growthbook_config.trackingCallback = (experiment, result) => {
                const expDataLayer = [];
                const experimentData = extractExperimentData(experiment, result);
                const currentExp = {
                    ...experimentData,
                    status: 'CLIENT_ASSIGNMENT'
                };
                expDataLayer.push(currentExp);
                updateDataLayer(expDataLayer);
                perfMark(`gb-script-tracking-end`);
                perfMeasure(`gb-script-tracking-finish`, `gb-script-end`, `gb-script-tracking-end`);
            };
            window.growthbook_config.noStreaming = true;
            // The SDK drains this queue after `growthbook.min.js` initializes a client instance.
            window.growthbook_queue = window.growthbook_queue || [];
            window.growthbook_queue.push((gb) => {
                const markReady = function () {
                    perfMark('gb-script-end');
                    perfMeasure('gb-script-ready', 'gb-script-start', 'gb-script-end');
                };
                if (gb.ready) {
                    markReady();
                    return;
                }
                // `growthbookdata` fires once the SDK finishes loading data, at which point gb.ready should be true.
                const onGrowthbookData = function () {
                    if (gb.ready) {
                        document.removeEventListener('growthbookdata', onGrowthbookData);
                        markReady();
                    }
                };
                document.addEventListener('growthbookdata', onGrowthbookData);
            });
        }
        catch (e) {
            console.error('GrowthBook config setup error:', e);
        }
        try {
            const stickyBrands = ['tatler', 'woi'];
            const isStickyBucketingEnabled = stickyBrands.includes(brandSlug) && !!userXid;
            if (isStickyBucketingEnabled) {
                localStorageXidCleanUp('gbStickyBuckets__', userXid);
            }
            if (clientSdkKey && apiHost && enableClient && userXid) {
                const cnDebug = getCookie(CookieAttributes.CN_DEBUG) || false;
                const s = document.createElement('script');
                s.async = true;
                s.dataset.clientKey = clientSdkKey;
                s.dataset.apiHost = apiHost;
                if (isStickyBucketingEnabled) {
                    s.dataset.useStickyBucketService = 'localStorage';
                    s.dataset.stickyBucketPrefix = 'gbStickyBuckets__';
                }
                s.dataset.uuid = userXid;
                s.dataset.enableDevMode = cnDebug.toString();
                s.src = `/verso/static/assets/growthbook.min.js`;
                document.head.appendChild(s);
                perfMark(`gb-script-start`);
            }
            else {
                console.info('SDK loading skipped - missing requirements:', {
                    hasClientSdkKey: !!clientSdkKey,
                    hasApiHost: !!apiHost,
                    enableClient,
                    hasExpId: !!userXid
                });
            }
        }
        catch (e) {
            console.error('GrowthBook SDK loading error:', e);
        }
    })({"userAuthenticated":false,"section":"skin","contentType":"article","hasBuyButtons":true,"clientSdkKey":"sdk-hDi6h5Y8vGWhIu","apiHost":"https://variants.conde.digital","enableClient":true,"brandSlug":"allure"});</script></head><body class="allure-us light onenav-site-navigation default"><noscript><iframe title="Google Tag Manager" src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/ns.html?id=GTM-WPC9DS6" height="0" width="0" style="display:none;visibility:hidden"></iframe></noscript><div id="app-root"><div><div class="BasePageWrapper-bRZGVW hUVQiw page ArticlePageBase-gybiYJ hZOlGC page--article"><div class="BasePageNavigationBackgroundFiller-iwwSIR geELrs"></div><div class="AdWrapper-fGiLaV iGDxYx BasePageAd-hwVUmA ekbFop ad ad--out-of-page"><div class="ad__slot ad__slot--out-of-page" data-node-id="lsvpz9"></div></div><div class="AdWrapper-fGiLaV iGDxYx BasePageAd-hwVUmA ekbFop ad ad--outstream"><div class="ad__slot ad__slot--outstream" data-node-id="sc3wndc"></div></div><div class="AdWrapper-fGiLaV iGDxYx BasePageAd-hwVUmA ekbFop ad ad--overlay"><div class="ad__slot ad__slot--overlay" data-node-id="9md5eh"></div></div><a href="#main-content" data-testid="BasePageSkipLink" class="BaseLink-haTOKm BasePageSkipLink-dQMpyE cOFTZe kWA-doN">Skip to main content</a><div class="InterstitialWrapper-hkIVaq ezgzgI"><aside class="PaywallModalWrapper-itMFEN fkdbJh paywall-modal paywall-modal--paywall"><div class="ConsumerMarketingUnitThemedWrapper-kjbXjp gnOkbl ConsumerMarketingUnitWrapper-ilIxPI ldqdbt paywall-modal__consumer-marketing-unit consumer-marketing-unit consumer-marketing-unit--paywall-modal-full-barrier" role="presentation" aria-live="assertive" aria-hidden="true"><div class="consumer-marketing-unit__slot consumer-marketing-unit__slot--paywall-modal-full-barrier"></div><div class="journey-unit"></div></div></aside></div><div class="OneNavSpacer-etugCY brOoOK theme-inverted" height="0"></div><header data-testid="one-nav-container-header_menu" class="OneNavContainer-kolMaZ